---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Home">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Vertically Integrated Project · UN SDG 7</span>
        <h1>Your campus is the lab.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          The GT Energy Solutions VIP is a for-credit research team, open to sophomores through PhD students in any major.
          You audit real Georgia Tech buildings, find where energy is being wasted, and recommend the fixes that campus
          planners use.
        </p>
        <div class="btn-row">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/the-vip">See what the team does</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/get-involved">Find your fit</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure class="photo">
        <img
          src="/images/vip-students.jpg"
          width="960"
          height="620"
          alt="About twenty Energy Solutions VIP students stand with their instructors inside a campus building, holding notebooks."
        />
        <figcaption>
          Students in the Fall 2025 Energy Solutions VIP course with their instructors. Photo:
          <a href="https://news.gatech.edu/news/2026/02/27/students-take-lead-campus-energy-decisions-through-hands-vip-course">Georgia Tech News</a>.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>The VIP at a glance</h2>
      <div class="stats">
        <div class="stat-tile">
          <strong>4</strong>
          <p>Campus buildings on Marietta Street that students audited in Fall 2025, using the industry-standard ASHRAE Level 1 method.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-tile">
          <strong>1–3</strong>
          <p>Credit hours per semester, for a letter grade. You can stay on the team for up to three years.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-tile">
          <strong>2050</strong>
          <p>The year Georgia Tech has committed to reach net-zero emissions. This team works on how to get there.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="cite">
        Sources:
        <a href="https://news.gatech.edu/news/2026/02/27/students-take-lead-campus-energy-decisions-through-hands-vip-course">GT News, Feb. 2026</a>;
        <a href="https://vip.gatech.edu/prospective-students/">VIP Program</a>;
        <a href="https://sustain.gatech.edu/2024/04/05/climate-action-plan-provides-road-map-to-net-zero-emissions/">GT Climate Action Plan</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What you’ll actually do</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="num">1</div>
          <h3>Audit real buildings</h3>
          <p>Walk mechanical rooms with building managers and measure how HVAC, lighting, water, and the building envelope perform.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="num">2</div>
          <h3>Recommend real upgrades</h3>
          <p>Your audit report goes to campus planning. They use it for future upgrades, cost savings, and return-on-investment estimates.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="num">3</div>
          <h3>Explore what’s next</h3>
          <p>In 2026–27, the team is evaluating hydrogen, energy storage, and renewable generation for the Georgia Tech campus.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">How VIP works</span>
        <h2>Research credit, starting sophomore year</h2>
        <p>
          <a href="https://president.gatech.edu/blog/power-vertically-integrated-projects-innovation-education-georgia-tech-world">Vertically Integrated Projects (VIP)</a>
          began at Georgia Tech in 2009. Each team mixes sophomores, seniors, and
          graduate students on one long-term project. Newer members learn from returning ones, who take on leadership
          roles as they go.
        </p>
        <p>
          This video from the Georgia Tech Research Institute shows what being on a VIP team is like. Then
          <a href="/the-vip">see how the Energy Solutions team applies that model to campus energy</a>.
        </p>
        <blockquote>
          “Our students are incredibly capable, and this course shows just how much they can contribute when given the
          opportunity.”
          <cite>Jennifer Chirico, Associate Vice President of Sustainability</cite>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
      <div class="video">
        <iframe
          src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/EmqrYSn5oNs"
          title="Creating a Pipeline of Future Technology Leaders (Georgia Tech Research Institute)"
          loading="lazy"
          allow="accelerometer; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
          referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
          allowfullscreen></iframe>
        <p class="cite">
          Video: “Creating a Pipeline of Future Technology Leaders,”
          <a href="https://gtri.gatech.edu/newsroom/vip-program">Georgia Tech Research Institute</a> (YouTube).
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Teams fill up. Apply early.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Applications for VIP open the semester before and close the first Thursday of classes. Not sure it’s for you?
        Take our two-question quiz. It also matches you with other campus sustainability projects.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/the-vip#apply">How to apply</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/get-involved#quiz">Take the quiz</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero,
  .cta {
    background:
      radial-gradient(900px 400px at 85% -10%, rgba(179, 163, 105, 0.35), transparent 60%),
      linear-gradient(160deg, var(--navy) 0%, var(--navy-deep) 100%);
    color: #fff;
  }
  .hero {
    padding: clamp(3.5rem, 9vw, 6rem) 0;
  }
  .hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr));
    align-items: center;
  }
  .hero h1,
  .cta h2 {
    color: #fff;
  }
  .hero .eyebrow {
    color: var(--gold);
  }
  .hero .lead,
  .cta .lead {
    color: #cfdbe7;
  }
  .photo {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .photo img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    box-shadow: 0 20px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
  }
  .photo figcaption {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: #b9c8d6;
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
  }
  .photo figcaption a {
    color: #fff;
  }
  blockquote {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--gold);
    background: var(--gold-soft);
    border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
    font-style: italic;
  }
  blockquote cite {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
</style>
